 "said": {
  "text": "What about skins? How's skins doing? Is skins gonna um, be upgraded since we've we've made um so many more asset types? ... Added into skins.",
  "verbatim": true,
  "at": "",
  "source": "voice",
  "by": "claude-voice",
  "addenda": [
   {
    "text": "Upgrade the skins system so it styles EVERY asset type now in the registry, not just the original kinds. Cover the new types: embeddable widget, icon pack, composite assets (button = box + text, nav = container + items), data set bar (search/filter/sort), embed, and every element down to text blocks/labels. Skins apply at any scope: global/app/UI/plugin, with child-overrides-parent inheritance (same model as design/icon packs). A skin is a design pack; it MAY reference an icon pack but doesn't have to. Pull the full asset-type list from the registry dynamically so new types are covered automatically going forward (no hardcoded list); add a CI check that fails if a registered asset type has no skin coverage. Voice + API/MCP/CLI parity. Submit at least 3 UI options to UI Review first.",
    "at": "",
    "source": "console",
    "verbatim": true
   }
  ]
 },
 "brief": "# Skins upgrade — cover all new asset types (Brett)\nUpgrade the skins system so it styles EVERY asset type now in the registry, not just the original kinds.\n- Cover the new types: embeddable widget, icon pack, composite assets (button = box + text, nav = container + items), data set bar (search/filter/sort), embed, and every element down to text blocks/labels.\n- Skins apply at any scope: global/app/UI/plugin, with child-overrides-parent inheritance (same model as design/icon packs).\n- A skin is a design pack; it MAY reference an icon pack but doesn't have to.\n- Pull the full asset-type list from the registry dynamically so new types are covered automatically going forward (no hardcoded list); add a CI check that fails if a registered asset type has no skin coverage.\n- Voice + API/MCP/CLI parity. Submit at least 3 UI options to UI Review first.",
